# Saw: "Whenever equipped creature attacks, ..." triggers only for the creature it is attached to, and with no permanent to
# offer (other than that creature and the Equipment) nothing is asked and nothing is drawn. Two Black Lotuses pay for Saw and
# Equip {2}, and are sacrificed doing it. Turn 3 the unequipped Ornithopter#2 attacks (no trigger - the equipped Ornithopter#1 would be
# a legal sacrifice, so a trigger would ask and draw); on turn 5 the equipped Ornithopter#1 attacks and the other Ornithopter is
# the one permanent offered: sacrificed, it draws the Lightning Bolt under the turn-five draw.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Saw
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Plains
Island
Island
Island
Lightning Bolt
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Saw.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Saw.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter#2 > Bot2)
? Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Hand = Plains; Island; Island
? Bot2.Life = 20
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter#1 > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter#1)
! Bot1.Choose(Saw)
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter#2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Hand = Plains; Island; Island; Island; Lightning Bolt
? Bot2.Life = 18

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Saw; Ornithopter
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Black Lotus; Black Lotus
Bot1.Hand = Plains; Island; Island; Island; Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Life = 18
